---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
---
<Layout title="AI Strategy Guides for Startups & Business | Pranjal Pandey" description="Start with the free AI Strategy Starter for Founders & Leaders. Practical resources for choosing workflows and making better AI decisions.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="guides-opening" aria-labelledby="guides-title">
      <div class="guides-promise">
        <p class="eyebrow">Guides & playbooks / Practical AI</p>
        <h1 id="guides-title">Choose the workflow.<br />Then the tool.</h1>
        <p class="lead">A free guide to choosing your first AI workflows, before building another pilot. For founders & leaders.</p>
        <ul class="guide-contents"><li>Five questions to ask before any AI project.</li><li>How to pick your first three workflows.</li><li>Why most AI pilots stall, and how to make yours stick.</li></ul>
        <p class="fine-print">By Pranjal Pandey. Founder, Taskflo AI. PhD researcher in multi-agent systems at IIT Jodhpur.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-signup-panel" id="free-guide" aria-labelledby="signup-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Free PDF + monthly letter</p>
        <h2 id="signup-title">Get the AI Strategy Starter.</h2>
        <p>Confirm your email to get the PDF.</p>
        <Signup id="guides-email" />
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section"><h2>On the writing desk.</h2><p class="lead">Two deeper playbooks are planned. Neither is for sale yet.</p><div class="offer-list">
      <article class="offer-row"><span class="mono">Upcoming</span><div><h3>AI for Startups</h3><p>The planned playbook for founders: where AI gives a small team leverage, what to build vs buy, how to keep costs sane, and how not to burn months on demos.</p></div></article>
      <article class="offer-row"><span class="mono">Upcoming</span><div><h3>AI for Business</h3><p>For managers and leadership teams: choosing the right AI projects, getting security and teams on board, and turning pilots into everyday workflows.</p></div></article>
    </div></section>
    <section class="close"><h2>Want to apply it to your own situation?</h2><p>A paid strategy session gives your question dedicated working time.</p><a class="button" href="/work/#sessions">Explore the sessions</a></section>
  </div>
</Layout>
